---
description: Fuse project-wide rules
alwaysApply: true
---

You are implementing Fuse, a hackathon prototype that proves one behavior: a
Bedrock-powered integrated agent can be stopped before its next model/tool
invocation after a policy violation.

Do not expand scope without explicit approval. Do not replace backend state with
frontend-only animation. Do not use real financial or personal data. Do not claim
exact billing, universal framework support, arbitrary-agent interception, or
cancellation of every already-running request.

Every changed behavior requires a test. Every user-visible claim must be supported
by an implemented behavior or labeled as a limitation. Prefer small typed modules,
explicit errors, deterministic fixtures, and least-privilege AWS permissions.

Work only in the current checkpoint. Stop when the checkpoint says STOP.
